x716 text "Iteration"
x717 puts x715 x716
x718 call close x717 
x719 call open x718 2
x720 write x719 2
x721 text "There are no loops in the body of a function. Repetition is fold and loop over an earlier function: the step function receives the state, the index, and any extra arguments, and returns the next state. loop adds a predicate function that is checked before each iteration. n may be a literal or a value. A literal count is bounded statically, against the per-function budget. A variable count is bounded by fuel in the reference interpreter; compiled targets have no execution budget, so it runs as many iterations as the value says."
