x809 puts x807 x808
x810 write x809 2
x811 text "# reply\n"
x812 puts x810 x811
x813 call close x812 
x814 write x813 2
x815 text "e0\nhi lt p2 a\nr select hi p2 a"
x816 puts x814 x815
x817 call close x816 
x818 call close x817 
x819 call close x818 
x820 call open x819 13
x821 write x820 4
x822 write x821 1
x823 text "diagnostics"
x824 puts x822 x823
x825 call open x824 11
x826 write x825 2
x827 text "Diagnostics"
x828 puts x826 x827
x829 call close x828 
x830 call open x829 2
x831 write x830 2
x832 text "Every rejection carries a stable code (parse, type, structure, handle, revision, limit), what was expected, what was seen, and the one fix that resolves it. The compiler never guesses: a reply that is ambiguous is rejected with the fix, not applied approximately."
x833 puts x831 x832
x834 call close x833 
x835 call close x834 
ret x835
end

fn sec_run io -> io
x837 call open p0 13
x838 write x837 4
x839 write x838 1
x840 text "bounds"
x841 puts x839 x840
x842 call open x841 11
x843 write x842 2
x844 text "Bounds and safety"
x845 puts x843 x844
x846 call close x845 
x847 call open x846 2
x848 write x847 2
x849 text "Static caps: 65536 functions per program (also after linking), 4096 instructions per function, 64 parameters, arrays up to 65536 elements (1024 on the hardware and GPU targets), literal iteration budget 2^24 per function. Variable iteration counts are bounded by fuel in the reference interpreter; compiled targets have no execution budget. io output is bounded by the caller's buffer. There is no heap, no recursion, no exceptions, and no undefined behavior: div and rem by zero are defined, shifts mask the count, indices wrap modulo the array length."
x850 puts x848 x849
x851 call close x850 
x852 call close x851 
x853 call open x852 13
x854 write x853 4
x855 write x854 1
x856 text "cli"
x857 puts x855 x856
